# DELETED 2026-08-22: superseded once system_power_announcement.yaml was
# cut over to this automation's v5 phrasing (see docs/ha-automations.md).
# Kept only as a reference/recreation copy — not live on the instance.
#
# Trial automation, created 2026-08-22 via the HA REST API
# (POST /api/config/automation/config/1787376439276). Live entity id:
# automation.mutatrack_power_comfort_announcement_trial
#
# Goal: replace the templated TTS announcement (system_power_announcement.yaml)
# with a more expressive one, reusing the ai_task/Ollama call pattern from the
# now-superseded daily summary automation (see docs/ha-automations.md). Runs
# in PARALLEL as a text notification for a few days of review before any
# decision to cut the spoken automation over.
#
# Same trigger/conditions as system_power_announcement.yaml, so it fires on
# the identical SOC-crossing events. Only the action differs.
#
# Entity ids containing "i30000251520943825" are this install's inverter
# serial-derived suffix — see the note in system_power_announcement.yaml.
#
# FIXED 2026-08-22 (post-creation): the first real trigger (SOC 29->30)
# errored before posting any notification — "value should be a string for
# dictionary value @ data['entity_id']". Root cause: entity_id was under a
# separate `target:` key instead of directly in `data:`, which is the
# pattern the working daily-summary automation uses (see
# mutatrack_daily_summary_via_ollama.yaml.superseded). Mixing `target` with
# this service caused HA to also inject a list-form entity_id into `data`,
# which the service schema rejects as needing a plain string.
#
# REWRITTEN 2026-08-22 (prompt v4, same day): the first real notification
# (SOC 39->40, daytime) came back garbled — the model (llama3.2
# 1b-instruct-q4_K_M, a small quantized local model) just echoed the raw
# prompt facts back in a degenerating, self-contradicting repeat loop
# instead of composing the requested sentences. Root cause: the original
# prompt asked the model to both reason about comfort/risk AND compose
# natural phrasing in one step — too much for a 1B model. Iterated
# directly against ai_task.generate_data (bypassing the automation, via
# `POST /api/services/ai_task/generate_data?return_response`) through
# several prompt versions:
#   v2: shortened instructions, still asked the model to reason about
#       comfort/risk itself -> coherent but sometimes hallucinated
#       numbers or refused to give a verdict ("it is not clear whether...")
#   v3/v4: comfort/risk verdict decided deterministically in the Jinja
#       template (mirrors the Home view's existing threshold logic on the
#       Sundial dashboard, see ha-config/dashboards/dashboard-powertrack.yaml)
#       — model's only job per branch is turning an already-decided outcome
#       into 1-2 short sentences. Consistent and coherent across repeated
#       test calls, but read as bland/static.
#
# REPLACED WITH STATIC RANDOMIZED PHRASING 2026-08-22 (v5, this version):
# asked for "more personality" — tested tone-instruction and few-shot-example
# prompt variants directly against ai_task.generate_data (bypassing the
# automation each time) to see if warmer phrasing was achievable. Both
# reintroduced the v1 failure modes (duplicated/rambling output, invented
# details like "it's getting pretty dark in this area", a hallucinated
# "75%" in place of the real SOC) more often than not — the 1B model's
# reliability ceiling is lower than the "bland but correct" v4 prompt was
# already sitting at. See docs/ha-automations.md's "Model capability
# findings" section for the full writeup, including why bigger local
# models aren't a viable fix on this hardware (measured ~104s for a
# trivial one-line prompt on the already-downloaded llama3.2:latest/3.2B —
# no GPU acceleration on this host).
#
# The LLM/ai_task call is removed entirely for now. Personality comes from
# a short hand-written list of phrasings per branch (same four branches as
# v4), picked at random via Jinja's `| random` filter — zero latency, zero
# hallucination risk, some rotation instead of the same sentence every
# time. This is the pragmatic stopgap until better (GPU-accelerated or
# hosted) hardware makes real LLM-generated phrasing viable again — see
# docs/ha-automations.md for what to revisit then.
alias: "MutaTrack Power Comfort Announcement (Trial)"
description: "Trial: hand-written comfort announcement (randomized per-branch phrasing), parallel to the spoken template"
triggers:
  - trigger: state
    entity_id: sensor.mutatrack_i30000251520943825_battsoc
conditions:
  - condition: template
    value_template: >
      {{ trigger.from_state is not none and
         trigger.to_state is not none and
         trigger.from_state.state not in ['unknown','unavailable'] and
         trigger.to_state.state not in ['unknown','unavailable'] }}
  - condition: template
    value_template: >
      {{ (trigger.from_state.state | int(0) // 10) != (trigger.to_state.state | int(0) // 10) }}
actions:
  - action: notify.persistent_notification
    data:
      title: "Power Comfort (Trial)"
      message: >
        {% set soc = trigger.to_state.state | int(0) %}
        {% set load = ((states('sensor.mutatrack_i30000251520943825_l1_phase_output_load_rate')|float(0) + states('sensor.mutatrack_i30000251520943825_loadpercent_l2')|float(0)) / 2) | round(0) %}
        {% set hour = now().hour %}
        {% set is_night = hour >= 21 or hour < 6 %}
        {% if soc == 100 %}
        {% set phrases = ["Battery's fully charged.", "You're topped off at 100 percent.", "Fully charged and ready to go."] %}
        {% elif is_night and soc < 40 and load > 25 %}
        {% set phrases = [
          "Battery's down to " ~ soc ~ " percent, and it's tight overnight -- worth easing off non-essentials.",
          "You're at " ~ soc ~ " percent with load running high; you could be cutting it close before sunrise.",
          soc ~ " percent and dropping fast -- might be worth switching off anything you don't need right now."
        ] %}
        {% elif is_night and soc < 40 %}
        {% set phrases = [
          "Battery's at " ~ soc ~ " percent, but load's light enough that you'll comfortably make it to sunrise.",
          "You're at " ~ soc ~ " percent overnight -- nothing to worry about with how little you're drawing right now.",
          soc ~ " percent and holding steady; you should coast through to sunrise just fine."
        ] %}
        {% else %}
        {% set phrases = ["Battery's at " ~ soc ~ " percent.", "You're sitting at " ~ soc ~ " percent right now.", "Charge level: " ~ soc ~ " percent."] %}
        {% endif %}
        {{ phrases | random }}
mode: single
